/-!
# Projective affine charts at a relatively flat point

Source: Stacks Project, More on Flatness, Tag 05ID,
`proposition-finite-presentation-flat-at-point`
(blueprint: lem-sfb-flat-point-projective-etale-source-chart).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A finitely presented quasi-coherent sheaf flat at a point has projective sections
on an affine elementary etale source neighbourhood over an affine elementary etale
base neighbourhood. The action on sections is restriction along `q.appTop`, with no
finite-generation condition over the base ring. The residue-field conditions concern
the actual induced maps, and the square is only required to commute.

Source: Stacks Project, More on Flatness, Tag 05ID,
`proposition-finite-presentation-flat-at-point`
(blueprint: lem-sfb-flat-point-projective-etale-source-chart).

Proof:
1. Choose affine opens $V\ni s$ and $W\ni x$ with $W\subseteq f^{-1}(V)$ by
   [lem-weil-pbc-affine-opens-basis]. Put $A=\Gamma(V,\mathcal O)$, $B=\Gamma(W,\mathcal O)$ and
   $M=\Gamma(W,F)$. The map $A\to B$ is finitely presented by
   [lem-weil-pbc-lfp-affine-opens-finite-presentation], and $M$ is finitely presented over $B$ by
   [lem-weil-pbc-finite-presentation-affine-sections]. The counit of
   [lem-weil-pbc-affine-tilde-gamma-adjunction] identifies $F|_W$ with $\widetilde M$. For $w\in
   W$ with primes $\mathfrak q_w\subset B$ and $\mathfrak p_w\subset A$,
   [lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-stalk-localization] and [lem-weil-pbc-spec-tilde-stalk-localization]
   identify the module stalk with $M_{\mathfrak q_w}$ and the base stalk with $A_{\mathfrak p_w}$,
   respecting the scalar action (both send a section to its germ). By
   [lem-weil-pbc-flat-over-localization], $M_{\mathfrak q_w}$ is flat over $A_{\mathfrak p_w}$
   exactly when it is flat over $A$. Thus [lem-weil-pbc-openness-of-flatness] gives an open
   $E\subseteq W$ consisting precisely of the points where $F$ is flat over $S$. The hypothesis
   gives $x\in E$.
2. Choose an affine open $U\ni x$ inside $E$ by [lem-weil-pbc-affine-opens-basis]. Keep
   $V=\operatorname{Spec}A$, replace $B$ by $\Gamma(U,\mathcal O)$, and put $M=\Gamma(U,F)$. Again
   [lem-weil-pbc-lfp-affine-opens-finite-presentation] and
   [lem-weil-pbc-finite-presentation-affine-sections] give that $A\to B$ and the $B$-module $M$
   are finitely presented. In particular $B$ is generated by finitely many algebra generators over
   $A$, and the cokernel presentation of $M$ supplies finitely many module generators. Write
   $\mathfrak q\subset B$, $\mathfrak p\subset A$ for $x,s$. Every stalk of $F|_U$ is flat over
   $V$: the open inclusion $V\subset S$ identifies its local rings with those of $S$. The
   restrictions retain quasi-coherence and finite presentation since their local presentations are
   the same on the smaller opens.
3. Apply [lem-trf-complete-algebra-devissage-etale-existence] to $A\to B,M,\mathfrak q$. Obtain a
   commutative square with rings $A_0,B_0$, primes $\mathfrak p_0,\mathfrak q_0$, etale spectrum
   maps $e_0:T_0=\operatorname{Spec}A_0\to V$ and $g_0:Y_0=\operatorname{Spec}B_0\to U$, and both
   specified residue-field isomorphisms. Let $q_0:Y_0\to T_0$ be the fourth map. Its marked points
   map to $x,s$ and to each other by the prime contractions in the cited statement. Put
   $H=g_0^*(F|_U)$ and $N_0=\Gamma(Y_0,H)$. The affine counit
   [lem-weil-pbc-affine-tilde-gamma-adjunction] and [lem-weil-pbc-tilde-pullback-base-change]
   identify $H$ with $\widetilde{B_0\otimes_B M}$ and $N_0$ with $B_0\otimes_B M$. The interchange
   $b_0\otimes m\mapsto m\otimes b_0$, inverse $m\otimes b_0\mapsto b_0\otimes m$, identifies this
   with the module in the cited existence theorem. Therefore $N_0/B_0/A_0$ has a complete algebra
   devissage over $\mathfrak p_0$.
4. The map $U\to V$ is locally of finite presentation: the affine finite presentation in step 2
   gives a single chart in the definition [def-sbc-locally-finite-presentation]. Apply
   [lem-sfb-scheme-etale-source-target-properties] with $P$ locally of finite presentation to the
   square in step 3. Its two horizontal maps are etale, so $q_0$ is locally of finite
   presentation. Since $Y_0,T_0$ are affine, [lem-weil-pbc-lfp-affine-opens-finite-presentation]
   gives that $A_0\to B_0$ is finitely presented. By [lem-weil-pbc-module-pullback-quasi-coherent]
   and [lem-pc-tensor-pullback-finite-presentation], $H$ is quasi-coherent and finitely presented.
   Thus [lem-weil-pbc-finite-presentation-affine-sections] makes $N_0$ finitely presented over
   $B_0$. We have imposed no finite-presentation condition on $N_0$ over $A_0$.
5. The etale map $g_0$ is flat by [def-weil-etale-morphism]. At every $z\in Y_0$,
   [lem-trf-relative-flatness-source-cover] applied to $g_0:Y_0\to U$ over $V$ and $F|_U$ shows
   that $H$ is flat over $V$ at $z$, using step 2. Put $t=q_0(z)$ and $v=e_0(t)$. The stalk $H_z$
   is an $\mathcal O_{T_0,t}$-module through $q_0$. Apply [lem-trf-etale-local-ring-flatness] to
   the etale $e_0:T_0\to V$ and this module: flatness over $\mathcal O_{V,v}$ implies flatness
   over $\mathcal O_{T_0,t}$. Consequently $H$ is flat over $T_0$ at every point. By
   [lem-pc-affine-chart-relative-flat-criterion] on the whole affine $Y_0$ over the affine $T_0$,
   $N_0$ is flat over $A_0$. This checks flatness over the new base without asserting that the
   square is cartesian.
6. Apply [lem-trf-complete-algebra-devissage-projective-localization] to $A_0\to B_0$, $N_0$, and
   $\mathfrak p_0$. Its hypotheses are finite presentation of the algebra and of the source module
   (step 4), flatness over $A_0$ (step 5), and the complete devissage (step 3). Obtain $a\in
   A_0\setminus\mathfrak p_0$ such that $(N_0)_a=N_0\otimes_{A_0}(A_0)_a$ is projective over
   $(A_0)_a$. The result allows arbitrary rank. In particular it requires neither finite
   generation nor finite presentation over $A_0$.
7. Let $b$ be the image of $a$ in $B_0$. Define $S'=D(a)\subset T_0$ and $Y=D(b)\subset Y_0$. They
   are affine with rings $(A_0)_a,(B_0)_b$ by
   [lem-weil-pbc-principal-localization-open-immersion]. The restriction $q:Y\to S'$ exists
   because the inverse image of $D(a)$ is $D(b)$. For the quasi-coherent $H$,
   [lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-affine-section-base-change] gives
   $\Gamma(Y,H|_Y)=N_0\otimes_{B_0}(B_0)_b$. This is canonically $N_0\otimes_{A_0}(A_0)_a$: both
   are the module of fractions $n/a^k$, with $n\otimes(c/b^k)\mapsto cn/a^k$ and $n/a^k\mapsto
   n\otimes 1/b^k$. These maps are well defined by the fraction relations and inverse on the
   displayed generators. For the composite $g:Y\to Y_0\to U\to X$,
   [lem-pc-module-pullback-identity-composition] identifies $g^*F$ with $H|_Y$ (pullback by an
   open inclusion is restriction by its tensor formula). Hence step 6 is exactly the required
   projectivity of $\Gamma(Y,g^*F)$ through $q$.
8. Since $a\notin\mathfrak p_0$ and $\mathfrak q_0\cap A_0=\mathfrak p_0$, also $b\notin\mathfrak
   q_0$. Thus both marked points remain in $S',Y$. The maps $Y\to Y_0$, $U\to X$, $S'\to T_0$, and
   $V\to S$ are open immersions; they are etale, and their composites with $g_0,e_0$ are etale by
   clauses (1)--(2) of [lem-weil-pbc-etale-composition-cancellation]. The new principal-open
   localizations preserve the marked residue fields by
   [lem-weil-pbc-localization-prime-residue-field-iso], clauses (1)--(3); the initial open
   restrictions $U\subset X,V\subset S$ also have identical local rings at their points, since the
   neighbourhoods contained in an open form a cofinal system for its stalk. Composing these
   isomorphisms with the residue isomorphisms of step 3 gives $\kappa(x)\cong\kappa(y)$ and
   $\kappa(s)\cong\kappa(s')$. The square remains commutative by restriction of the square of step
   3. These maps and points give every clause of the statement. -/
theorem exists_projective_affine_etale_source_chart
    {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) [LocallyOfFinitePresentation f]
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [F.IsFinitePresentation] (x : X)
    (hflat : Module.Flat (S.presheaf.stalk (f x))
      ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars (f.stalkMap x).hom).obj
        ((RingedSpace.moduleStalkFunctor X.toRingedSpace x).obj F))) :
    ∃ (Y S' : Scheme.{u}) (y : Y) (s' : S')
      (g : Y ⟶ X) (q : Y ⟶ S') (e : S' ⟶ S),
      IsAffine Y ∧ IsAffine S' ∧ g ≫ f = q ≫ e ∧ g y = x ∧ q y = s' ∧
      Etale g ∧ IsIso (g.residueFieldMap y) ∧
      Etale e ∧ IsIso (e.residueFieldMap s') ∧
      @Module.Projective Γ(S', ⊤) _ Γ((Scheme.Modules.tensorPullback g).obj F, ⊤) _
        (Module.compHom _ q.appTop.hom) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
